  "id": "COMPOUND:17730 - PROTEIN:3858",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential mechanistic link between Boehmenan and Tumor necrosis factor receptor superfamily member 10B, mediated through DNA polymerase alpha subunit B. Multiple paths indicate that Boehmenan targets this subunit, which is then inhibited by various compounds (Stemanthrene D, 3R,5S-Sonnerlactone, and 2,3-Dihydroauriculatin), all of which ultimately target the tumor necrosis factor receptor superfamily member 10B. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust, albeit indirect, relationship, with each compound acting as a bridge in the pathway. The presence of multiple distinct compounds targeting the same downstream target implies that the mechanism may involve different modes of action, possibly through distinct molecular interactions. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Boehmenan modulates the tumor necrosis factor receptor superfamily member 10B via the DNA polymerase alpha subunit B, though further validation with direct evidence of compound-target interactions or genetic markers would be necessary to confirm the specificity and biological relevance of this relationship.",
